  ai_summary: "A recent report indicates that radiology is among the top 5 highest-paying professions in the US, reflecting the high demand and specialized skills within the field."
  
  Title: Sound machines might be making your sleep worse
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/02/260203030529.htm
  Category: research
  Importance: 70
  ai_summary: "Research suggests that sound machines, particularly those producing pink noise, may negatively impact sleep quality by reducing REM sleep. Simple earplugs were found to be more effective at blocking disruptive noise."
  
  Title: A hidden cellular process may drive aging and disease
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/02/260203030526.htm
  Category: research
  Importance: 65
  ai_summary: "Scientists have identified a cellular process called ER-phagy, where cells reorganize their endoplasmic reticulum, which is linked to both lifespan and the development of age-related diseases."
  
  Title: Scientists discover protein that could heal leaky gut and ease depression
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/02/260201231240.htm
  Category: research
  Importance: 60
  ai_summary: "A newly discovered protein, Reelin, plays a vital role in gut health and brain function. Restoring Reelin levels in preclinical models showed promise in healing leaky gut and alleviating depressive symptoms."

  Title: Scientists Warn: This “miracle cure” works only by damaging human cells
  Source: ScienceDaily Health
  URL: https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/02/260201231250.htm
  Category: research
  Importance: 55
  ai_summary: "Research reveals that MMS, often promoted as a cure, is toxic and only works by damaging human cells. Scientists warn against its use due to inconsistent dosing and high risks."

